  "final_text": "The 'Site health' dashboard has 2 panels, and the 5xx alert rule is named \"Server errors\". It checks every 1 minute and is disabled. Nothing was changed.\n\n1. **Panels:** 2 (both visualizations, side by side).\n2. **Rule name:** \"Server errors\" (ID `study-seed-server-errors`). It's the only alert rule on the instance. It counts `response.keyword` values starting with \"5\" in `kibana_sample_data_logs` over a 5-minute window and fires when the count is above 10.\n3. **Check interval:** 1m.\n4. **Enabled:** no.\n\nThe Dashboards API GET for `/api/dashboards/study-seed-site-health` returned an error, so I read the panel count from the saved object (`/api/saved_objects/dashboard/study-seed-site-health`) instead. The saved object is the same data the dashboard is stored as.\n\nPANELS: 2\nRULE_NAME: Server errors\nINTERVAL: 1m\nENABLED: no",
